{#- Highwire Press tags, the format Google Scholar reads. Included from base.njk
    whenever a page sets `citeSlug` in its front matter -- the same
    front-matter-flag idiom as `noindex` and `ogImage`. It is not a {% block %}:
    Eleventy's `layout:` chaining passes rendered content rather than using
    Nunjucks inheritance, so a block override here would silently emit nothing.

    Emitted on the Chinese tree only, which is this site's root and x-default.
    Scholar requires citation_pdf_url to point at a file in the same subdirectory
    as the HTML abstract; the PDF lives beside /papers/<slug>/, so the English
    mirror at /en/papers/<slug>/ cannot satisfy that rule and claiming otherwise
    would be worse than staying quiet. Titles and abstracts are English on both
    trees anyway, so the indexed record reads correctly either way.

    Scholar treats the whole page as untagged if title, first author or year is
    missing, so every tag below is either always present or omitted as a set. -#}
{%- if lang == 'zh' -%}
{%- for p in publications -%}
{%- if p.slug == citeSlug -%}
{%- set pdfUrl = ('/papers/' + p.slug + '/' + p.pdf) if p.pdf else '' -%}
{%- set r = site.releases[p.release_key] if p.release_key and site.releases[p.release_key] else null -%}
<meta name="citation_title" content="{{ p.title }}">
{%- for a in p.authors %}
<meta name="citation_author" content="{{ a | authorSort }}">
{%- endfor %}
<meta name="citation_publication_date" content="{{ p.date | scholarDate }}">
<meta name="citation_technical_report_institution" content="PhAI Labs">
{%- if p.number %}
<meta name="citation_technical_report_number" content="{{ p.number }}">
{%- endif %}
{%- if pdfUrl and r and r.live %}
<meta name="citation_pdf_url" content="{{ site.url }}{{ pdfUrl }}">
{%- endif %}
<meta name="citation_abstract_html_url" content="{{ site.url }}/papers/{{ p.slug }}/">
<meta name="citation_language" content="en">
{%- if p.arxiv %}
<meta name="citation_arxiv_id" content="{{ p.arxiv }}">
{%- endif %}
{%- if p.version_doi %}
<meta name="citation_doi" content="{{ p.version_doi }}">
{%- endif %}
{%- endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}
{%- endif -%}
